subQuestions.answerMdx:
Keep `var` but pass `i` into a small function (a factory or an IIFE) so each call receives its own copy:
`for (var i = 0; i < tabs.length; i++) {
  (function (n) {
    tabs[n].addEventListener('click', () => console.log('Tab ' + n))
  })(i)
}`
The parameter `n` is a new binding created on every call, so each handler closes over that call's `n` (0, 1, 2). Because `n` is a function parameter it is never mutated by later iterations, so the values stay correct.

subQuestions.answerMdxZh:
保留 `var`，但把 `i` 传进一个小函数（工厂函数或 IIFE），让每次调用拿到自己的副本：
`for (var i = 0; i < tabs.length; i++) {
  (function (n) {
    tabs[n].addEventListener('click', () => console.log('Tab ' + n))
  })(i)
}`
参数 `n` 在每次调用时都会新建一个绑定，所以每个处理器闭包捕获的是那次调用的 `n`（0、1、2）。因为 `n` 是函数参数，不会再被后续迭代修改，所以值始终正确。

